<p>The "E" in E2B and E4B stands for "effective" parameters. The smaller mo=
dels incorporate Per-Layer Embeddings (PLE) to maximize parameter efficienc=
y in on-device deployments. Rather than adding more layers or parameters to=
 the model, PLE gives each decoder layer its own small embedding for every =
token. These embedding tables are large but are only used for quick lookups=
, which is why the effective parameter count is much smaller than the total=
.</p>
